<BaseLayout
  title="Atocha Cercanías one stop into Sol — four doors before 14:00 | Dubliners"
  description="Sunday 8 Nov: arrive Atocha by train, ride Cercanías C3/C4 one stop to Sol, then walk to Victoria 6, Espoz y Mina 7 and Pasaje de Matheu 4 before 14:00. Station geography, Maps, distances. Not Metro, not Barajas."
  path={PATH}
  lang="en"
  hreflang={{ en: PATH, es: PATH_ES }}
  ogImage="/images/facade.jpg"
  extraJsonLd={[articleLd, faqLd]}
>
  <section class="hero hero-compact" data-show-until={SHOW_UNTIL}>
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb current="Atocha Cercanías one stop into Sol, then the four doors" schema />
      <h1>Atocha Cercanías: one stop into Sol, then pin the four doors before 14:00</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Saturday is over. You did not land at Barajas, you are not on a Metro platform, and you did not check out of a Sol hotel.
        <strong>You arrived by train at Atocha</strong> — AVE, Alvia, or a Cercanías change at Atocha-Cercanías.
        Ride <strong>C3 or C4 one stop north to Sol</strong> (~2–3 min when the line is running). Exit the Sol Cercanías concourse toward Carrera de San Jerónimo / Calle de Carretas, then the south-east pocket.
        Pin the four sister doors before Four Corner opens at 14:00 with sports screens (about five hours from 09:00; not open before). Maps below.
      </p>
      <p class="small">En español: <a href={withBase(PATH_ES)} hreflang="es" lang="es">Atocha Cercanías: una parada a Sol, luego las cuatro puertas antes de las 14:00</a></p>
      <FanWeekendCtas lang="en" findHref="/visit/" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>This is a train-station hop, not Metro Sol, not Barajas, not Plaza Mayor</h2>
      <p>
        Other pages already cover the first Sunday Metro into the L1/L2/L3 station, a late Barajas taxi, a Sol hotel’s first street,
        Plaza Mayor’s east arcade downhill, and a stroll out from the square itself.
        This page is only for the person <strong>coming off a long-distance or commuter train at Atocha</strong>
        who needs Cercanías line names, concourse exits, metres, and which door to pin before 14:00.
        Do not re-promote Saturday 18:00–19:00 or Valencia–Real Madrid as still on.
      </p>

      <h2>Atocha-Cercanías → Sol — one stop, then which exit</h2>
      <p>
        Puerta de Atocha (long-distance) connects underground to <strong>Atocha-Cercanías</strong>.
        From there, <strong>Cercanías C3 or C4</strong> run one stop north to <strong>Sol</strong> — a different station from Metro Sol.
        We do not invent a first-train clock: ride when Sunday Cercanías is running.
        At Sol, stay in the <strong>Cercanías concourse</strong> (not the Metro corridors). Exit toward
        <strong>Carrera de San Jerónimo</strong> and <strong>Calle de Carretas</strong> — that heading is the south-east pocket of the square.
        Then Espoz y Mina, Pasaje de Matheu (the covered cut-through) and Calle de la Victoria.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>From Sol Cercanías exits.</strong>
          Espoz y Mina 7: <strong>3–5 min / 220–320 m</strong>.
          Pasaje de Matheu 4: <strong>4–5 min / 250–350 m</strong>.
          Victoria 6: <strong>4–6 min / 280–380 m</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Optional walk from Atocha, skip the one stop.</strong>
          North on <strong>Calle de Atocha</strong> past Antón Martín to Plaza de Jacinto Benavente, then Calle de Carretas to the same south-east hop.
          About <strong>18–22 min / 1.4–1.6 km</strong>. Useful if you already have bags on the street and would rather not re-enter the concourse.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        From about 09:00 it is <strong>about five hours</strong> until Four Corner opens at 14:00.
        Pin Victoria 6 for that hour. Do not camp a closed door on Calle de la Victoria before then.
      </p>

      <h2>Before 14:00 — which door is even open</h2>
      <p>
        Four Corner opens <strong>Sunday 8 November from 14:00 until late, with sports screens</strong>.
        Not before 14:00. We do not list which game is on there — ask at the door.
        O’Reilly’s usual from 11:30 (Pasaje de Matheu 4). Dubliners and O’Connell’s from 12:00 (Espoz y Mina 7).
        Ride the one stop now; sit the first sister that is open; be on Victoria for the 14:00 open.
        Premier League from 15:00 (Palace–Liverpool, Sunderland–Chelsea, Brighton–Brentford, Ipswich–Bournemouth),
        United–Villa 17:30, NFL afternoon/evening, and Atlético–Barcelona 21:00 sit on the same streets after that — coordinate, do not substitute.
        Named listings: Dubliners <a href={withBase('/whats-on/')}>What’s On</a> only. Ask which screen — not every game on every screen.
      </p>

      <h2>Concourse to three streets — addresses</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Four Corner — Calle de la Victoria 6, 28012 Madrid</strong> (pin for 14:00; sports screens; not open before).
          About 4–6 min from Sol Cercanías.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.fourCorner} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.fourCorner} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Reilly’s Restaurant Bar — Pasaje de Matheu 4, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          Covered passage off Espoz y Mina. Usual from 11:30. About 4–5 min from Sol Cercanías.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.oreillys} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.oreillys} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Dubliners — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          About 3–5 min from Sol Cercanías. Sunday from 12:00. Named screens on What’s On — ask which game is on.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.dubliners} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.dubliners} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Connell’s — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, 28012 Madrid</strong> (Maps listing: O’Connell St).
          Same street number as Dubliners, different door. Sunday 8 Nov from 12:00 (usual Sunday 14:00). Meeting point; we do not invent its board.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.oconnell} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.oconnell} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <OriginalFourBars lang="en" when="sunday" findHref="/visit/" />

      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <dl class="faq">
        <dt><strong>Off a train at Atocha this morning. Metro Sol? Which way?</strong></dt>
        <dd>Cercanías, not Metro. C3/C4 one stop to Sol. Exit toward San Jerónimo / Carretas. Pin Victoria 6 for 14:00. Then Matheu 4 and Espoz y Mina 7 twice.</dd>
        <dt><strong>How far from Atocha / Sol Cercanías to the four doors?</strong></dt>
        <dd>From Sol Cercanías: Espoz y Mina 7 3–5 min / 220–320 m; Matheu 4 4–5 min / 250–350 m; Victoria 6 4–6 min / 280–380 m. Walk from Atocha: 18–22 min / 1.4–1.6 km north on Calle de Atocha.</dd>
        <dt><strong>It is ~09:00. Is Four Corner open?</strong></dt>
        <dd>No. From 14:00, sports screens — about five hours from now. O’Reilly’s from 11:30; Dubliners and O’Connell’s from 12:00. Do not wait on Victoria 6 before 14:00.</dd>
      </dl>

